Z||000000||rider||12-05-2000||09:45 AM||||Is it possible to retro fit a TTop or sun roof to an 85GT?<P>||||reg||1
Z||000001||alpha||12-05-2000||10:03 AM||||It is really easy to add a sunroof to a solid roof car. You just need a fiber roof section, the glass, the seal, the latch and maybe the headliner (you can modify a solid roof one).<P>T-tops require some welding (I think) and the parts are really expensive, but it can be done as well. I think Tim Perrigo still is selling complete conversion kits.<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://fiero.dhs.org/fiero/sig.jpg">   <BR>   <A HREF="mailto:douglas_knight@umit.maine.edu">douglas_knight@umit.maine.edu</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Tina||12-05-2000||10:09 PM||||Uhh, that reminds me off the Sunroof from the junkjard.<BR>Asked the guys to please remove it,would be by later to pick it up.<BR>Just make sure you don't leave any parts behind.<BR>2 hours later.<BR>Well where is it?<BR>Around the corner!<BR>Why outside?<BR>Then I saw it  "gulp<BR>What you don't want it anymore?<BR>"Gulp"  ......There it was the entire , and I mean the whole roof.<BR>And the worst part the thing was riveted in with what looked like a million rivets.<BR>You did say you wanted all the parts! <P>No, I didn't take it. Glad too.Because I found a Fiero with T-Tops a month later.<BR>Now I just have to transpant them into my good car this winter.<P>Tina||||reg||1
Z||000003||mbramble||12-06-2000||07:48 AM||||As stated by Alpha above, you just need to find a donor car that has a sunroof.  Here is a link to some instructions for doing the swap.  I went through the process a couple months ago.  <BR> <A HREF="http://www.cyberverse.com/~cyco/fieroparts/tips/sunroof.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.cyberverse.com/~cyco/fieroparts/tips/sunroof.htm</A> ||||reg||1
